#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:5
msgid "Install with `npm install rimraf`, or just drop rimraf.js somewhere."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:7
msgid "API"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:9
msgid "`rimraf(f, [opts], callback)`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:11
msgid ""
"The first parameter will be interpreted as a globbing pattern for files. "
"If you want to disable globbing you can do so with `opts.disableGlob` "
"(defaults to `false`). This might be handy, for instance, if you have "
"filenames that contain globbing wildcard characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:16
msgid ""
"The callback will be called with an error if there is one.  Certain "
"errors are handled for you:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:19
msgid ""
"Windows: `EBUSY` and `ENOTEMPTY` - rimraf will back off a maximum of "
"`opts.maxBusyTries` times before giving up, adding 100ms of wait between "
"each attempt.  The default `maxBusyTries` is 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:22
msgid ""
"`ENOENT` - If the file doesn't exist, rimraf will return successfully, "
"since your desired outcome is already the case."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:24
msgid ""
"`EMFILE` - Since `readdir` requires opening a file descriptor, it's "
"possible to hit `EMFILE` if too many file descriptors are in use. In the "
"sync case, there's nothing to be done for this.  But in the async case, "
"rimraf will gradually back off with timeouts up to `opts.emfileWait` ms, "
"which defaults to 1000."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:30
msgid "options"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:32
msgid ""
"unlink, chmod, stat, lstat, rmdir, readdir, unlinkSync, chmodSync, "
"statSync, lstatSync, rmdirSync, readdirSync"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:35
msgid ""
"In order to use a custom file system library, you can override   specific"
" fs functions on the options object."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:38
msgid ""
"If any of these functions are present on the options object, then   the "
"supplied function will be used instead of the default fs   method."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:42
msgid "Sync methods are only relevant for `rimraf.sync()`, of course."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:44
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:52
msgid "maxBusyTries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:54
msgid ""
"If an `EBUSY`, `ENOTEMPTY`, or `EPERM` error code is encountered   on "
"Windows systems, then rimraf will retry with a linear backoff   wait of "
"100ms longer on each try.  The default maxBusyTries is 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:58 ../../source/rimraf_README.md:69
msgid "Only relevant for async usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:60
msgid "emfileWait"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:62
msgid ""
"If an `EMFILE` error is encountered, then rimraf will retry   repeatedly "
"with a linear backoff of 1ms longer on each try, until   the timeout "
"counter hits this max.  The default limit is 1000."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:66
msgid ""
"If you repeatedly encounter `EMFILE` errors, then consider using   "
"[graceful-fs](http://npm.im/graceful-fs) in your program."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:71
msgid "glob"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:73
msgid "Set to `false` to disable [glob](http://npm.im/glob) pattern   matching."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:76
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Set to an object to pass options to the glob module.  The default   glob "
"options are `{ nosort: true, silent: true }`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:79
msgid "Glob version 6 is used in this module."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:81
msgid "Relevant for both sync and async usage."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:83
msgid "disableGlob"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:85
msgid ""
"Set to any non-falsey value to disable globbing entirely.   (Equivalent "
"to setting `glob: false`.)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:88
msgid "rimraf.sync"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:90
msgid ""
"It can remove stuff synchronously, too.  But that's not so good.  Use the"
" async API.  It's better."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:93
msgid "CLI"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/rimraf_README.md:95
msgid ""
"If installed with `npm install rimraf -g` it can be used as a global "
"command `rimraf <path> [<path> ...]` which is useful for cross platform "
"support."
msgstr ""

